{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-328248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(6x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,\\frac{1}{6}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-328248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 6x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=\\frac{1}{12}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-328248" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "930da8780d27cad57130fcbab5b665d777b5a80a16239ee586891c2b6ad997be"} {"question" "q-328248" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-328248" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-328419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(5x+{75}^{∘})=-1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx={a}^{∘}+n\\cdot {36}^{∘},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{36}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-328419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+{75}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & ={135}^{∘}-{75}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={12}^{∘}+n\\cdot {36}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-328419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "930da8780d27cad57130fcbab5b665d777b5a80a16239ee586891c2b6ad997be"} {"question" "q-328419" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-328419" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x+{12}^{∘})=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation is\n\n$$\nx={8}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{60}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{60}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+{12}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n6x+{12}^{∘}={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,6x+{12}^{∘}={120}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ={60}^{∘}-{12}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,6x & ={120}^{∘}-{12}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 6x & ={48}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,6x & ={108}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={8}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\,x & ={18}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={18}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329515" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "930da8780d27cad57130fcbab5b665d777b5a80a16239ee586891c2b6ad997be"} {"question" "q-329515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329515" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +4\\pi n,\\,x=-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+4\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $(-4,0].$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n,\\,\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =-\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2}=-\\frac{7\\pi }{12}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =-\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+4\\pi n, & \\, & x=-\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+4\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have that $a=-\\frac{11}{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "930da8780d27cad57130fcbab5b665d777b5a80a16239ee586891c2b6ad997be"} {"question" "q-329544" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-329544" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{11}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-331964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{4\\pi n}{3},\\,x=a\\pi +\\frac{4\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the interval $[0,\\frac{4}{3}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-331964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & \\frac{3x}{2} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & \\frac{3x}{2} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{4\\pi n}{3} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+\\frac{4\\pi n}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=\\frac{7}{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-331964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "930da8780d27cad57130fcbab5b665d777b5a80a16239ee586891c2b6ad997be"} {"question" "q-331964" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"} {"question" "q-331964" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987349/state.json" "file_sha256" "9795e1f193e4cc6f32069ebefa198aa2026491d96912d89c790c769dc91cb0eb"}] "usage" {} "basis" 947 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
